---
import Container from "../shared/Container.astro";
import Paragraph from "../shared/Paragraph.astro";
import Title from "../shared/Title.astro";
---

<section class="relative py-16 md:py-20" id="philosophy">
    <Container className="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
        <div class="text-center space-y-4">
            <Title>
                Why Agentic Development Needs a New Foundation
            </Title>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6">
            <Paragraph>
                AI is transforming software development — but most teams are simply bolting AI tools onto existing processes. The result? Unreliable outputs, no verification, and wasted potential. <strong>Agentic development</strong> demands more than clever prompts; it requires a deliberate process — and tools built specifically for human-AI collaboration.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                That process has two distinct phases. The first — <strong>design and specification</strong> — is inherently collaborative and interactive. Teams workshop requirements, make architectural decisions, and produce precise design documents together. This is where human creativity, domain knowledge, and judgement are irreplaceable.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                The second phase — <strong>implementation</strong> — is where AI agents take over. But autonomous execution demands determinism: properly configured coding agents, automated test suites, architectural compliance checks, and continuous evaluation of agent performance on real project scenarios. Without these guardrails, you're just generating code and hoping for the best.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                We help teams bridge both phases. Through <strong>consulting</strong>, we identify bottlenecks in your current process and guide you step by step toward a more effective workflow — from configuring coding agents to designing verification pipelines. Through our <strong>tools</strong>, we provide the deterministic foundation that makes autonomous implementation reliable: architecture extraction from code, agent evaluation frameworks, and structured knowledge for AI consumption.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
        </div>
    </Container>
</section>
